# You will need to have PlaceholderAPI installed for the placeholders to work. You can download it from https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/placeholderapi.6245/
# You will also need to have the PlaceholderAPI expansion for Skript, which can be installed using the command /papi ecloud download skript in-game.

# Anything which is a variable can be changed to fit your server's needs, such as the name of the currency or the items in the shop.
# If you use this code on your minecraft server, please consider giving credit to the original creator, which is me, as it took a lot of time and effort to create this code. Thank you.

placeholderapi placeholder with the prefix "<Your World Name>":
    if the identifier is "<Your Currency Name>":
        set the result to {<Your Currency Name>.%player%}
        if {<Your Currency Name>.%player%} is not set:
            set {<Your Currency Name>.%player%} to 0

